# CONTINUOUS NATIVE GENERATION, COMMITTED (#996 CNG wave; #1011).
#
# `ios/` and `android/` are OUTPUTS of `expo prebuild`, and they are TRACKED —
# not ignored. Everything this app decides about them still lives in
# `app.config.ts`, the config plugins under `plugins/`, and the autolinked local
# modules under `modules/`; committing the result is what makes a native change
# arrive as a reviewable diff instead of as a hash nobody can read.
#
# So there is no rule for either tree here, on purpose. A rule over a tracked
# tree is the worst of both worlds: the files stay committed while the next
# regeneration never shows up in `git status`, which is the one thing this
# arrangement exists to show. `apps/mobile/ios/.gitignore` and
# `apps/mobile/android/.gitignore` — themselves prebuild outputs — carry the
# build artefacts each tree produces.
#
# A file that has to survive a regeneration is still a file a plugin must write:
# prebuild overwrites a hand-edit, and `ci:native-state`'s L1 fails the drift.
